# UI framework patterns (must follow)

## Layered architecture

- **Actions** go in `tests/ui/actions/*Actions.ts` and are constructed via the `action` fixture.
- **Pages** go in `tests/ui/pages/*Page.ts` and expose **typed Element getters only** (no assertions, no business logic).
- **Element behaviour lives on the element itself**, not in a procedural action layer.

## Use the framework primitives

- In **Pages**, build typed elements via the surface locator with a role:
  ```ts
  get nameInput() {
    return surfaceLocator("Name input")
      .asTextInput()
      .desktop(p => p.locator("input[name='name']"))
      .build(this.page, this.surface);
  }
  ```
  Available roles: `.asButton()`, `.asTextInput()`, `.asCheckbox()`, `.asDropdown()`, `.asFileInput()`. Omit a role for spans/labels/toasts (defaults to `GenericElement`).
- In **Actions**, drive the UI through the element directly:
  - Interactions / waits: `page.btn.click()`, `page.input.clearAndFill(v)`, `page.cb.check()`, `page.x.waitForVisible()`, `page.x.hover()`, `page.x.scrollIntoView()`
  - Reads: `page.list.count()`, `page.row.text()`, `page.x.attribute(name)`, `page.x.isVisible()`
  - Assertions: `page.x.expect.toBeVisible()`, `page.x.expect.toHaveText(...)`, `page.x.expect.not.toBeChecked()`
  - Escape hatch: `page.x.run("Label", loc => loc.exoticMethod(...))`
- Page-/context-level helpers stay procedural in `ActionDeps`:
  - `nav.goto(...)`, `nav.reload(...)`, `nav.waitForURL(...)`
  - `pageAssert.urlContains(...)`, `pageAssert.titleIs(...)`
  - `dialogs.*`, `frames.*`, `storage.*`

## Boundaries (don't mix responsibilities)

- **Do not** embed `expect(...)` assertions directly in Pages — use `element.expect.*` from the Action.
- **Do not** use `page.locator(...)` directly inside Actions — extend the Page object with a typed element getter.
- **Do not** add a procedural action wrapper layer (no `UIActions`-style classes, no `ui.click(element)` patterns). Drive elements through their own methods.
- Keep Actions methods **task-level** (intent-based), not tiny "click this one selector" helpers unless reused.

## Fixtures

- When adding new Actions, register them in `tests/ui/support/action.fixture.ts`.
